All solid convex polygons are homeomorphic to each other because they are all topologically equivalent to a closed 2D disk. A convex polygon's interior and boundary can be continuously deformed into a disk, and their boundaries (which are polygons) are homeomorphic to a circle. Since all disks are homeomorphic regardless of their specific shape (triangle, square, etc.), the topological space is the closed unit disk.

**Final Answer**
